{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Elohim dealt well with the midwives.</b> From what? From 'and the people multiplied greatly.' And they were not suspected of bloodshed. And from the fact that Pharaoh had no inclination to harm them — he said in his heart: they are only two midwives, they cannot manage to deliver all the women of so great a people; surely it is as they say — before the midwife comes to them, they give birth."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:42.766647307Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}